/** @mainpage Qore geos Module

    @tableofcontents

    @section geosintro Introduction

    The geos module provides <a href="https://libgeos.org">GEOS (Geometry Engine - Open Source)</a> bindings for
    %Qore, enabling fast GIS data processing with spatial predicates, topology operations, spatial indexing, and
    WKT/WKB/GeoJSON serialization.

    This module is released under the MIT license (see COPYING.MIT in the source distribution for more information).

    The module is tagged as such in the module's header (meaning it can be loaded unconditionally regardless of how
    the %Qore library was initialized).

    Like all Qore components, the geos module is thread-safe. Each thread lazily initializes its own GEOS context
    handle using the reentrant GEOS C API (\c _r variants).

    The underlying geometry functionality is provided by <a href="https://libgeos.org">GEOS (libgeos)</a>.

    The module has two layers:
    - <b>C++ binary module</b> (\c geos): GEOSGeometry, GEOSPreparedGeometry, GEOSSTRtree, and
      WKT/WKB/GeoJSON reader/writer classes for in-memory geometry operations
    - <b>@ref geosdataproviderintro "GEOSDataProvider"</b>: data provider integration for reading and
      writing WKT/WKB/GeoJSON geometry files in data pipelines (load with \c %%requires \c GEOSDataProvider)

    @section geosclasses Classes

    The following classes are provided:
    - @ref Qore::GEOS::GEOSGeometry "GEOSGeometry" - Core geometry wrapper with spatial predicates, topology
      operations, distance calculations, simplification, validation, linear referencing, coordinate access,
      triangulation, hull operations, and WKT/WKB/GeoJSON serialization
    - @ref Qore::GEOS::GEOSPreparedGeometry "GEOSPreparedGeometry" - Pre-indexed geometry for fast repeated
      spatial queries (contains, intersects, within, touches, crosses, overlaps, disjoint, distance, relate)
    - @ref Qore::GEOS::GEOSSTRtree "GEOSSTRtree" - STR-packed R-tree spatial index for envelope intersection
      queries, nearest-neighbor searches, and iteration
    - @ref Qore::GEOS::GEOSWKTReader "GEOSWKTReader" - WKT parsing
    - @ref Qore::GEOS::GEOSWKTWriter "GEOSWKTWriter" - WKT serialization with formatting options
    - @ref Qore::GEOS::GEOSWKBReader "GEOSWKBReader" - WKB parsing (binary and hex)
    - @ref Qore::GEOS::GEOSWKBWriter "GEOSWKBWriter" - WKB serialization (binary and hex)
    - @ref Qore::GEOS::GEOSGeoJSONReader "GEOSGeoJSONReader" - GeoJSON parsing (since 1.1)
    - @ref Qore::GEOS::GEOSGeoJSONWriter "GEOSGeoJSONWriter" - GeoJSON serialization (since 1.1)

    @section geosfunctions Standalone Functions

    - @ref Qore::GEOS::geos_version() "geos_version()" - Returns the GEOS version string
    - @ref Qore::GEOS::get_geos_info() "get_geos_info()" - Returns detailed GEOS version information
    - @ref Qore::GEOS::parse_wkt() "parse_wkt()" - Convenience WKT parsing
    - @ref Qore::GEOS::make_wkt() "make_wkt()" - Convenience WKT serialization
    - @ref Qore::GEOS::parse_wkb() "parse_wkb()" - Convenience WKB parsing
    - @ref Qore::GEOS::make_wkb() "make_wkb()" - Convenience WKB serialization
    - @ref Qore::GEOS::parse_geojson() "parse_geojson()" - Convenience GeoJSON parsing (since 1.1)
    - @ref Qore::GEOS::make_geojson() "make_geojson()" - Convenience GeoJSON serialization (since 1.1)
    - @ref Qore::GEOS::geos_create_point() "geos_create_point()" - Create point from coordinates (since 1.1)
    - @ref Qore::GEOS::geos_create_linestring() "geos_create_linestring()" - Create linestring from coordinates (since 1.1)
    - @ref Qore::GEOS::geos_create_polygon() "geos_create_polygon()" - Create polygon from coordinate rings (since 1.1)
    - @ref Qore::GEOS::geos_create_collection() "geos_create_collection()" - Create geometry collection (since 1.1)
    - @ref Qore::GEOS::geos_create_empty_collection() "geos_create_empty_collection()" - Create empty collection (since 1.1)
    - @ref Qore::GEOS::geos_create_rectangle() "geos_create_rectangle()" - Create rectangle from bounds (since 1.1)
    - @ref Qore::GEOS::geos_relate_pattern_match() "geos_relate_pattern_match()" - Test DE-9IM pattern match (since 1.1)
    - @ref Qore::GEOS::geos_polygonize() "geos_polygonize()" - Build polygons from linework (since 1.1)
    - @ref Qore::GEOS::geos_cluster_dbscan() "geos_cluster_dbscan()" - DBSCAN spatial clustering (since 1.1)
    - @ref Qore::GEOS::geos_orientation_index() "geos_orientation_index()" - Point orientation test (since 1.1)
    - @ref Qore::GEOS::geos_segment_intersection() "geos_segment_intersection()" - Line segment intersection (since 1.1)

    @section geosconstants Constants

    - @ref geos_geometry_type_constants "Geometry Type Constants" - integer constants for geometry type
      identification (\c GEOS_POINT, \c GEOS_LINESTRING, \c GEOS_POLYGON, etc.)
    - @ref geos_make_valid_constants "MakeValid Method Constants" - repair methods
      (\c GEOS_MAKE_VALID_LINEWORK, \c GEOS_MAKE_VALID_STRUCTURE)
    - @ref geos_buffer_style_constants "Buffer Style Constants" - cap and join styles for buffering
      (\c GEOSBUF_CAP_ROUND, \c GEOSBUF_CAP_FLAT, \c GEOSBUF_JOIN_MITRE, etc.)

    @section geostypes Type Mappings

    |!GEOS Type|!Qore Type
    |Coordinate|\c hash<GEOSCoordinate>
    |Extent (bounding box)|\c hash<GEOSExtent>
    |Geometry|@ref Qore::GEOS::GEOSGeometry "GEOSGeometry"
    |WKT string|\c string
    |WKB data|\c binary
    |GeoJSON string|\c string

    @section geosexamples Examples

    @par Create a geometry from WKT and perform operations:
    @code{.py}
%modern
%requires geos

GEOSGeometry poly = new GEOSGeometry("POLYGON ((0 0, 10 0, 10 10, 0 10, 0 0))");
GEOSGeometry point = new GEOSGeometry("POINT (5 5)");

printf("contains: %y\n", poly.contains(point));  # True
printf("area: %y\n", poly.area());                # 100.0
printf("centroid: %y\n", make_wkt(poly.centroid())); # "POINT (5 5)"
    @endcode

    @par Create geometries programmatically (since 1.1):
    @code{.py}
GEOSGeometry pt = geos_create_point(1.0, 2.0);
GEOSGeometry rect = geos_create_rectangle(0, 0, 10, 20);
GEOSGeometry line = geos_create_linestring(({"x": 0, "y": 0}, {"x": 10, "y": 10}));
    @endcode

    @par Use GeoJSON I/O (since 1.1):
    @code{.py}
GEOSGeometry geom = parse_geojson('{"type":"Point","coordinates":[1,2]}');
string json = make_geojson(geom);
string json_pretty = geom.toGeoJSON(2);  # pretty-printed
    @endcode

    @par Simplify and validate geometries (since 1.1):
    @code{.py}
GEOSGeometry invalid = parse_wkt("POLYGON ((0 0, 10 10, 0 10, 10 0, 0 0))");
printf("valid: %y (%s)\n", invalid.isValid(), invalid.isValidReason());
GEOSGeometry fixed = invalid.makeValid();
GEOSGeometry simple = complex_poly.topologyPreserveSimplify(1.0);
    @endcode

    @par Use prepared geometry for fast repeated queries:
    @code{.py}
GEOSGeometry poly = new GEOSGeometry("POLYGON ((0 0, 10 0, 10 10, 0 10, 0 0))");
GEOSPreparedGeometry pg = poly.prepare();
for (int i = 0; i < 1000; ++i) {
    GEOSGeometry pt = parse_wkt(sprintf("POINT (%d %d)", i % 10, i / 100));
    if (pg.contains(pt)) {
        # handle contained point
    }
}
    @endcode

    @par Use STRtree for spatial indexing:
    @code{.py}
GEOSSTRtree tree(10);
tree.insert(parse_wkt("POINT (1 1)"), "A");
tree.insert(parse_wkt("POINT (2 2)"), "B");
tree.insert(parse_wkt("POINT (100 100)"), "C");

list<auto> results = tree.query(parse_wkt("POLYGON ((0 0, 5 0, 5 5, 0 5, 0 0))"));
# results contains "A" and "B"
    @endcode

    @par Transform coordinates with a callback (since 1.1):
    @code{.py}
GEOSGeometry poly = parse_wkt("POLYGON ((0 0, 10 0, 10 10, 0 10, 0 0))");
# shift all coordinates by (100, 200)
GEOSGeometry shifted = poly.transformXY(sub (float x, float y) { return (x + 100, y + 200); });
    @endcode

    @par Read geometry from a WKT file using the GEOSDataProvider module:
    @code{.py}
%modern
%requires GEOSDataProvider

# Read WKT file (one geometry per line)
GEOSWktReadDataProvider provider({"path": "shapes.wkt"});
map printf("%s: %s\n", $1.type, $1.geometry), provider.searchRecords();

# Write geometries to a WKB hex file
GEOSWkbWriteDataProvider writer({"path": "output.wkb"});
writer.createRecord({"geometry": "POLYGON ((0 0, 10 0, 10 10, 0 10, 0 0))"});

# Read/write GeoJSON (since 1.1)
GEOSGeoJsonReadDataProvider json_reader({"data": '{"type":"Point","coordinates":[1,2]}'});
map printf("%s\n", $1.type), json_reader.searchRecords();
    @endcode

    See the @ref geosdataproviderintro "GEOSDataProvider module documentation" for more examples.

    @section geosbuilding Building

    The geos module requires the GEOS library with C API headers to build.

    @subsection geosbuildreqs Build Requirements

    |!Distribution|!Packages
    |Ubuntu / Debian|\c libgeos-dev
    |Fedora / RHEL|\c geos-devel
    |Alpine|\c geos-dev

    @subsection geosbuildsteps Build Steps

    @code{.sh}
    mkdir build
    cd build
    cmake ..
    make
    make install
    make test
    @endcode

    If Qore or GEOS cannot be found automatically:
    @code{.sh}
    cmake .. -DQORE_DIR=/path/to/qore -DGEOS_DIR=/path/to/geos
    @endcode

    @section geosreleasenotes Release Notes

    @subsection geos_1_1 geos Module Version 1.1

    <b>New Features and Bug Fixes</b>
    - <b>Programmatic geometry construction</b>: geos_create_point(), geos_create_linestring(),
      geos_create_polygon(), geos_create_collection(), geos_create_empty_collection(),
      geos_create_rectangle()
    - <b>GeoJSON I/O</b>: GEOSGeoJSONReader, GEOSGeoJSONWriter classes; parse_geojson(),
      make_geojson() convenience functions; GEOSGeometry::toGeoJSON() method;
      GeoJSON DataProvider read/write classes for data pipeline integration
    - <b>Geometry properties</b>: isRing(), isClosed(), hasZ(), geometryTypeId(), getDimensions(),
      getXMin/YMin/XMax/YMax(), getExtent(), getX/Y/Z(), normalize(), equalsExact()
    - <b>Polygon decomposition</b>: getExteriorRing(), getInteriorRingN(), getNumInteriorRings(),
      getStartPoint(), getEndPoint(), getPointN()
    - <b>Validity and repair</b>: isValidReason(), isValidDetail(), makeValid(),
      makeValidWithParams(), pointOnSurface()
    - <b>Simplification</b>: simplify(), topologyPreserveSimplify()
    - <b>DE-9IM spatial relationships</b>: relate(), relatePattern(), geos_relate_pattern_match()
    - <b>Buffer with style</b>: bufferWithStyle(), offsetCurve() with cap/join style constants
    - <b>Distance metrics</b>: hausdorffDistance(), hausdorffDistanceDensify(),
      frechetDistance(), frechetDistanceDensify(), distanceWithin(), distanceIndexed()
    - <b>Unary union</b>: unaryUnion() for dissolving geometry collections
    - <b>Line operations</b>: lineMerge(), lineMergeDirected(), lineSubstring(), reverse(),
      node(), clipByRect(), snap()
    - <b>Triangulation and Voronoi</b>: delaunayTriangulation(),
      constrainedDelaunayTriangulation(), voronoiDiagram()
    - <b>Hull operations</b>: concaveHull(), concaveHullByLength(), polygonHullSimplify()
    - <b>Advanced analysis</b>: maximumInscribedCircle(), largestEmptyCircle(),
      minimumRotatedRectangle(), minimumWidth(), minimumBoundingCircle(),
      minimumClearance(), minimumClearanceLine()
    - <b>Polygonize and precision</b>: geos_polygonize(), buildArea(), setPrecision(),
      getPrecision()
    - <b>Coordinate transformation</b>: transformXY() with Qore closure callback
    - <b>Clustering</b>: geos_cluster_dbscan() DBSCAN spatial clustering
    - <b>Coverage operations</b>: coverageUnion(), coverageSimplifyVW(), coverageIsValid()
    - <b>Prepared geometry</b>: 12 additional predicates (within, touches, crosses, overlaps,
      disjoint, distance, distanceWithin, containsXY, intersectsXY, nearestPoints,
      relate, relatePattern)
    - <b>STRtree enhancements</b>: build(), iterate()
    - <b>Misc utilities</b>: extractUniquePoints(), sharedPaths(), removeRepeatedPoints(),
      densify(), geos_orientation_index(), geos_segment_intersection()
    - <b>Constants</b>: geometry type IDs, MakeValid methods, buffer cap/join styles
    - <b>Hashdecls</b>: GEOSExtent

    @subsection geos_1_0 geos Module Version 1.0

    <b>New Features and Bug Fixes</b>
    - Initial release
    - Classes: GEOSGeometry, GEOSPreparedGeometry, GEOSSTRtree, GEOSWKTReader,
      GEOSWKTWriter, GEOSWKBReader, GEOSWKBWriter
    - Standalone functions: geos_version(), get_geos_info(), parse_wkt(), make_wkt(),
      parse_wkb(), make_wkb()
    - Hashdecls: GEOSCoordinate, GEOSVersionInfo
    - Thread-safe implementation using reentrant GEOS C API
    - Cooperative cancellation support in STRtree queries
    - @ref geosdataproviderintro "GEOSDataProvider" separated module with WKT and WKB data providers
      for use in data pipelines
*/
